{"code":"29-1123.00","title":"Physical Therapists","description":"Assess, plan, organize, and participate in rehabilitative programs that improve mobility, relieve pain, increase strength, and improve or correct disabling conditions resulting from disease or injury.","jobZone":5,"kinds":{"R":{"score":4.33,"share":0.1977},"I":{"score":4.87,"share":0.2298},"A":{"score":2.17,"share":0.0695},"S":{"score":5.91,"share":0.2916},"E":{"score":2.49,"share":0.0885},"C":{"score":3.07,"share":0.1229}},"highPoints":["S","I","R"],"tasks":[{"id":363,"text":"Plan, prepare, or carry out individually designed programs of physical treatment to maintain, improve, or restore physical functioning, alleviate pain, or prevent physical dysfunction in patients.","core":true,"importance":4.79,"relevance":100,"frequency":6.4},{"id":364,"text":"Perform and document an initial exam, evaluating data to identify problems and determine a diagnosis prior to intervention.","core":true,"importance":4.78,"relevance":100,"frequency":5.48},{"id":370,"text":"Record prognosis, treatment, response, and progress in patient's chart or enter information into computer.","core":true,"importance":4.73,"relevance":100,"frequency":6.24},{"id":365,"text":"Evaluate effects of treatment at various stages and adjust treatments to achieve maximum benefit.","core":true,"importance":4.69,"relevance":100,"frequency":6.22},{"id":367,"text":"Instruct patient and family in treatment procedures to be continued at home.","core":true,"importance":4.69,"relevance":100,"frequency":5.42},{"id":368,"text":"Confer with the patient, medical practitioners, or appropriate others to plan, implement, or assess the intervention program.","core":true,"importance":4.69,"relevance":100,"frequency":5.96},{"id":366,"text":"Administer manual exercises, massage, or traction to help relieve pain, increase patient strength, or decrease or prevent deformity or crippling.","core":true,"importance":4.67,"relevance":100,"frequency":6.29},{"id":371,"text":"Obtain patients' informed consent to proposed interventions.","core":true,"importance":4.66,"relevance":97.3,"frequency":5.39},{"id":373,"text":"Test and measure patient's strength, motor development and function, sensory perception, functional capacity, or respiratory or circulatory efficiency and record data.","core":true,"importance":4.62,"relevance":100,"frequency":5.92},{"id":377,"text":"Direct, supervise, assess, and communicate with supportive personnel.","core":true,"importance":4.62,"relevance":97.3,"frequency":6.15},{"id":369,"text":"Review physician's referral and patient's medical records to help determine diagnosis and physical therapy treatment required.","core":true,"importance":4.6,"relevance":100,"frequency":5.43},{"id":374,"text":"Identify and document goals, anticipated progress, and plans for reevaluation.","core":true,"importance":4.57,"relevance":97.43,"frequency":5.62},{"id":375,"text":"Provide information to the patient about the proposed intervention, its material risks and expected benefits, and any reasonable alternatives.","core":true,"importance":4.41,"relevance":100,"frequency":5.57},{"id":381,"text":"Provide educational information about physical therapy or physical therapists, injury prevention, ergonomics, or ways to promote health.","core":true,"importance":4.38,"relevance":97.06,"frequency":4.99},{"id":20407,"text":"Inform patients and refer to appropriate practitioners when diagnosis reveals findings outside physical therapy.","core":true,"importance":4.37,"relevance":99.77,"frequency":3.25},{"id":372,"text":"Discharge patient from physical therapy when goals or projected outcomes have been attained and provide for appropriate follow-up care or referrals.","core":true,"importance":4.34,"relevance":97.43,"frequency":4.48},{"id":378,"text":"Administer treatment involving application of physical agents, using equipment, moist packs, ultraviolet or infrared lamps, or ultrasound machines.","core":true,"importance":3.9,"relevance":10